TY.md` (LOOK appended), `STYLE.md` (from VOICE), `MEMORY.md` and `examples/`, and warns when the license is outside the allowlist in `export.rs`.","startLine":74,"endLine":74,"text":"owo export soulspec writes soul.json, SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md (LOOK appended), STYLE.md (from VOICE), MEMORY.md and examples/, and warns when the license is outside the allowlist in export.rs."},{"markdown":"`--scenario <name>` sets `scenario` from that entry's summary. `--png` writes the avatar with the card in `tEXt` chunks: `chara` (V2 JSON, base64) always and `ccv3` (V3) for V3 cards, replacing earlier ones.","startLine":76,"endLine":76,"text":"--scenario <name> sets scenario from that entry's summary. --png writes the avatar with the card in tEXt chunks: chara (V2 JSON, base64) always and ccv3 (V3) for V3 cards, replacing earlier ones."},{"markdown":"`owo export skill --out <dir>` writes a `SKILL.md` that loads the identity with `owo context` and lists the read and write commands.","startLine":78,"endLine":78,"text":"owo export skill --out <dir> writes a SKILL.md that loads the identity with owo context and lists the read and write commands."},{"markdown":"Host-agnostic session sync: the host calls `sync start` after each turn and `sync done` after a successful ingest run.","startLine":82,"endLine":82,"text":"Host-agnostic session sync: the host calls sync start after each turn and sync done after a successful ingest run."},{"markdown":"`owo sync start --session <id> --transcript <path> [--format jsonl|claude-jsonl|opencode-json] [--every N] [--now]` parses user and assistant text, reads the bookmark in `<root>/.owo/sessions/<id>.json`, and counts new user turns. A run is due at `--every` turns (default `identity.json` `sync_every`, else 6), or at any new turn with `--now`.","startLine":84,"endLine":84,"text":"owo sync start --session <id> --transcript <path> [--format jsonl|claude-jsonl|opencode-json] [--every N] [--now] parses user and assistant text, reads the bookmark in <root>/.owo/sessions/<id>.json, and counts new user turns. A run is due at --every turns (default identity.json sync_every, else 6), or at any new turn with --now."},{"markdown":"When due it writes the slice, with two earlier user turns as overlap, to `<root>/sources/<slug>/<date>_<session>_<from>-<until>.md`, and the ingest prompt to `.owo/sessions/<id>.prompt.md`. `owo sync done --session <id> --until <n>` moves the bookmark forward; `--until` may not pass the message count the last `sync start` read. The prompt names the absolute root and runs `context --no-touch`, so ingest runs do not count as project sessions. `--project` must name an existing project. A file with no user or assistant messages for the chosen format fails. While a run is pending, a not-due `sync start` names its prompt.","startLine":86,"endLine":86,"text":"When due it writes the slice, with two earlier user turns as overlap, to <root>/sources/<slug>/<date>_<session>_<from>-<until>.md, and the ingest prompt to .owo/sessions/<id>.prompt.md. owo sync done --session <id> --until <n> moves the bookmark forward; --until may not pass the message count the last sync start read. The prompt names the absolute root and runs context --no-touch, so ingest runs do not count as project sessions. --project must name an existing project. A file with no user or assistant messages for the chosen format fails. While a run is pending, a not-due sync start names its prompt."},{"markdown":"`owo sync push --session <id> [--turns <json>] [--every N] [--now]` is for hosts with no transcript on this machine, such as a hosted chat over MCP. It takes a JSON array of `{id, role, text}` turns (stdin when `--turns` is left out), appends those whose id is not stored yet to `.owo/sessions/<id>.turns.jsonl`, then runs the `sync start` logic on that file. One bad turn fails the push and stores nothing; a session that syncs a local file refuses pushes. The reply adds `added` and, when due, `source_text` and `prompt_text`.","startLine":88,"endLine":88,"text":"owo sync push --session <id> [--turns <json>] [--every N] [--now] is for hosts with no transcript on this machine, such as a hosted chat over MCP. It takes a JSON array of {id, role, text} turns (stdin when --turns is left out), appends those whose id is not stored yet to .owo/sessions/<id>.turns.jsonl, then runs the sync start logic on that file. One bad turn fails the push and stores nothing; a session that syncs a local file refuses pushes. The reply adds added and, when due, source_text and prompt_text."},{"markdown":"The readers keep each message's id (`id` in jsonl, `uuid` in claude-jsonl, `id` in opencode-json), and slice headings show it after the message number.","startLine":90,"endLine":90,"text":"The readers keep each message's id (id in jsonl, uuid in claude-jsonl, id in opencode-json), and slice headings show it after the message number."}],"blocks":[{"type":"heading","start":0,"end":5,"startLine":1,"endLine":1,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":7,"end":121,"startLine":3,"endLine":3,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":123,"end":132,"startLine":5,"endLine":5,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":134,"end":235,"startLine":7,"endLine":7,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":237,"end":587,"startLine":9,"endLine":9,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":589,"end":600,"startLine":11,"endLine":11,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":602,"end":680,"startLine":13,"endLine":13,"children":[]},{"type":"list","start":682,"end":4136,"startLine":15,"endLine":34,"children":[{"type":"listItem","start":682,"end":809,"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","start":684,"end":809,"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"children":[]}]},{"type":"listItem","start":810,"end":1155,"startLine":16,"endLine":16,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","start":812,"end":1155,"startLine":16,"endLine":16,"children":[]}]},{"type":"listItem","start":1156,"end":1354,"startLine":17,"endLine":17,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","start":1158